  "description": "The smallest bike in our offering isn’t your average kid's bike. Developed personally by our CEO and tested by his son, it has our own ‘pro kids’ geometry. You will see the aggressive stance that a kid takes on this bike and the confidence with which the young rider will tackle difficult terrain. The Eccentric 20 is fitted with a cockpit specially designed for smaller hands – the JUNIT ProTaper handlebar and complementary grips have reduced diameter. Short cranks with a narrow Q – Factor are critical for efficient pedaling. The fork is also an important component specially designed for kids – it’s lightweight, sensitive and has a 15mm thru-axle. Light, fast rolling tires are mounted on wide rims can be run at really low pressures, making the bike very comfortable and stable on bumpy terrain. The Eccentric 20 is the way to go for kids who are serious about mountain biking.\nMAIN FEATURES:\n- Tough and light alloy frame w/New-school kid's geometry\n- Properly scaled-down modern geo with slack angles\n- RST Spex 20, 80mm travel, 15mm bolt axle, Air spring,\n- Hydrualic Rebound & Compression Adjust\n- Protaper unit handlebar with a reduced grip diameter\n- Hydraulic disc brakes\n- Kids specific crankset with narrow Q-factor\n- Light and strong tubeless compatible rims\n- Lightweight sealed bearing hubs\n- High volume fast-rolling tires\nFRAME | alloy\nFORK | Rst Spex 20, 80mm travel,\nDERAILLEUR | sram gx 1x10\nBRAKES | LANXI NUTT\nCRANKSET | ns bikes jUNIOr 127mm 28t\nHANDLEBAR | PROTAPER unit 600mm 20MM\nSTEM | NS bikes drop\nHUBS | ns bikes\nRIMS | ns bikes junior 24h\nTIRES | kenda sbe 20 x 2.1\"",
